equality_why: honest = shift(1)*ret and peek = signal*ret.shift(-1) are the SAME PnL stream shifted by one bar (identical non-NA products, different timestamps); equal NAV is NOT evidence that peek is look-ahead-free — both use next-period returns aligned to a prior signal; same-bar signal*ret WOULD be look-ahead.
